WEBVTT

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:07.025 --> 01:09.694
-Someone's hacking the security system.
-What do they want?

01:09.778 --> 01:11.738
Who is it? Russia? Or North Korea?

01:11.821 --> 01:14.407
They're finding out now.
We should rush over.

01:34.469 --> 01:36.096
SHOCK

01:36.179 --> 01:37.931
SEDUCTION

01:57.826 --> 01:58.952
Sleep well?

02:01.162 --> 02:01.996
Let's kiss.

02:03.164 --> 02:04.874
I need to plant onions.

02:14.843 --> 02:16.094
Goodness me.

02:17.470 --> 02:18.972
Done with the onions? Let's kiss.

02:19.681 --> 02:22.642
Hold up. I left that thing back there.
Silly me.

03:04.392 --> 03:05.768
You came back for this coffin?

03:06.352 --> 03:09.063
-You've found it now, so let's kiss--
-Wait up. Stop.

03:09.147 --> 03:12.400
This isn't something you can
just do whenever, you know?

03:13.401 --> 03:14.861
You like rules, don't you?

03:14.944 --> 03:17.155
These things have rules too.

03:17.238 --> 03:19.741
-What are those rules?
-Well, those rules are…

03:22.076 --> 03:23.244
First, the weather.

03:23.328 --> 03:25.205
Rain. It must be raining.

03:25.788 --> 03:26.664
Not yesterday.

03:27.832 --> 03:29.626
It was the first time yesterday.

03:30.126 --> 03:32.212
First kisses tend to be

03:32.295 --> 03:34.923
more spontaneous,
less restricted by the rules.

03:35.006 --> 03:37.508
But it must be raining for the second one.

03:38.092 --> 03:39.802
And there must be alcohol.

03:39.886 --> 03:42.013
Just after a drink. Right then.

03:44.349 --> 03:45.600
It's that complex?

03:45.683 --> 03:47.894
It's even more complex. I simplified it.

03:48.394 --> 03:49.771
Now close this back up.

03:52.023 --> 03:54.150
You're really mixing identities like this?

04:07.538 --> 04:09.249
The first digit has changed again.

04:10.333 --> 04:11.668
That fucking psycho bitch.

04:13.044 --> 04:14.879
KI KA-YOUNG
BALANCE: 20,688,348,652 WON

04:16.798 --> 04:18.383
And what's all this?

04:18.466 --> 04:20.218
ESTIMATED ASSETS
4,300,431,074 WON

04:20.301 --> 04:21.844
MONTHLY BILL
34,074,250 WON

04:27.225 --> 04:29.894
CHEONGPUNGHO BANK

04:29.978 --> 04:31.980
LUNCH BREAK
12 P.M. TO 1 P.M.

04:34.816 --> 04:37.777
Ms. Gu, weren't you classmates
with Ki Ka-young and Choi Min-ji?

04:38.278 --> 04:40.113
-Yes.
-Did you see their bags?

04:40.196 --> 04:41.364
They're both Hermès.

04:42.407 --> 04:44.742
She's just letting it sit on the floor.

04:45.285 --> 04:47.662
Hey, could we get two iced Americanos?

04:50.498 --> 04:52.625
He always does that
when we're headed to lunch.

04:52.709 --> 04:54.752
You go ahead.
I'll take a soybean paste stew.

04:55.253 --> 04:58.214
You really should open
a retirement savings fund account.

04:58.298 --> 05:00.800
The earlier you plan for retirement,
the better.

05:00.883 --> 05:03.136
I'm good. I don't need retirement.

05:04.262 --> 05:06.764
What do you mean
you don't need retirement?

05:06.848 --> 05:10.601
It's just Ms. Ki prefers
aggressive investments over low-risk ones.

05:10.685 --> 05:12.729
Of course, I understand.

05:13.396 --> 05:16.399
We should give you our new towel sets.
Ms. Gu? Where are they?

05:17.775 --> 05:18.609
Did you forget?

05:19.569 --> 05:22.405
Come on, Ms. Gu.
You should take more initiative.

05:23.072 --> 05:24.699
I'll bring them right over.

05:24.782 --> 05:27.118
Back to the topic of retirement, well…

05:27.201 --> 05:30.246
How should I explain this?
The profitability…

05:39.714 --> 05:44.052
As of today, construction is complete.
I just need a move-in date.

05:45.303 --> 05:46.304
Do you like it?

05:46.846 --> 05:47.805
Yes, Dad.

05:56.356 --> 05:58.024
Daddy!

05:58.524 --> 06:00.068
Goodness, you're blinding me!

06:00.151 --> 06:02.153
My darling princess,
did you study hard today?

06:02.236 --> 06:05.156
Like my life depended on it.
I'm tired as hell.

06:05.239 --> 06:08.201
I was paired up
with the transfer student today.

06:08.284 --> 06:09.869
-And?
-He's really cute.

06:09.952 --> 06:13.122
He is? Did he become
the apple of your eye, Princess?

06:13.206 --> 06:14.916
He seems really classy.

06:14.999 --> 06:17.085
-So I asked where he lived.
-And?

06:17.168 --> 06:19.754
-He lives in the mansion we talked about.
-Over there?

06:19.837 --> 06:21.464
-Yeah.
-They moved in?

06:21.547 --> 06:23.925
If they've moved in,
they should at least say hi.

06:24.926 --> 06:26.761
Guess we'll have to make a house call.

06:26.844 --> 06:28.012
Open up!

06:37.105 --> 06:38.606
Wait, those rules

06:39.148 --> 06:40.525
were this accurate?

06:44.195 --> 06:47.031
Genie, tell me about tomorrow's weather.

06:47.115 --> 06:48.241
Why would you ask me?

06:48.324 --> 06:50.535
Weather is a touchy subject
for me right now!

06:50.618 --> 06:53.371
Why are you making such a fuss
when I asked Genie?

06:54.122 --> 06:56.457
Genie, so what's the weather
like tomorrow?

06:56.541 --> 06:59.585
It's set to be a clear and sunny day
in Cheongpung tomorrow.

06:59.669 --> 07:00.503
Hear that?

07:01.337 --> 07:04.257
You should try asking it something.
It's so accurate.

07:10.179 --> 07:11.556
Hey. Other Genie.

07:12.348 --> 07:15.101
What does Ki Ka-young ask about the most?

07:15.768 --> 07:18.688
Here is a list of Ms. Ki Ka-young's
recent search history.

07:18.771 --> 07:22.900
Rainmaking ritual, artificial rain,
alcohol content of different beers,

07:22.984 --> 07:25.361
cool-toned lip tint,
lightning-fast delivery,

07:25.445 --> 07:28.781
rainmaking ritual…

07:28.865 --> 07:31.325
What the hell have you done, you idiot?

07:35.580 --> 07:37.540
Find out when it will rain this week.

07:37.623 --> 07:40.835
I just checked since the cherry blossom
festival starts tomorrow.

07:40.918 --> 07:42.795
Luckily, this entire week will be clear.

07:42.879 --> 07:44.088
Damn it, why?

07:45.923 --> 07:47.133
What about next week?

07:48.509 --> 07:51.721
The spring rain hits next week,
so Monday may be the only dry day.

07:51.804 --> 07:54.056
-Monday will be dry?
-Would you like it not to be?

07:54.640 --> 07:55.600
You can do that?

07:57.518 --> 08:00.062
-Since you're a mythical beast?
-I couldn't do it myself.

08:00.146 --> 08:01.481
But I can try praying.

08:05.193 --> 08:06.819
Not exactly useful.

08:07.403 --> 08:10.114
What is this about?
Please put the wrench down.

08:12.742 --> 08:13.659
Is something there?

08:14.243 --> 08:15.244
I'm pretty today.

08:20.416 --> 08:21.292
Pretty.

08:24.795 --> 08:25.838
Pretty.

08:29.383 --> 08:32.011
It's like the town is broke or something.

08:32.094 --> 08:34.055
Why couldn't they get IU
for the festival--

08:34.138 --> 08:35.097
What are you doing?

08:36.098 --> 08:37.058
Put that down!

08:40.895 --> 08:41.729
I'm pretty.

08:43.272 --> 08:44.941
Even prettier than before.

08:45.024 --> 08:46.609
Goodness, young lady.

08:47.235 --> 08:49.779
There are mirrors all over this house!

08:56.994 --> 08:59.497
It's not your fault, Master.

09:01.165 --> 09:04.544
Psychopaths tend to be
pretty narcissistic.

09:05.670 --> 09:06.587
Is that true?

09:07.296 --> 09:08.214
Thank goodness.

09:08.297 --> 09:10.883
I thought I must have
made her pretty somehow.

09:10.967 --> 09:13.052
I was pretty awesome in the moment.

09:13.135 --> 09:15.805
Why did I pick that moment
to get all competitive?

09:16.389 --> 09:17.765
What are you talking about?

09:18.266 --> 09:20.351
Now is the prime moment
to get competitive.

09:20.434 --> 09:22.395
That kiss was the gateway to corruption.

09:22.478 --> 09:24.605
Right. It should be, but…

09:25.982 --> 09:27.275
After 1,000 years,

09:28.276 --> 09:29.944
it was practically my first kiss.

09:31.529 --> 09:32.738
I almost died from nerves.

09:33.614 --> 09:36.033
I just feel bad for Ejllael.

09:36.117 --> 09:39.495
I hear he hits the gym nonstop
because he wants to slit your throat.

09:39.579 --> 09:42.748
Had he known a kiss would floor you,
he could've avoided all that effort.

09:43.374 --> 09:46.335
By the way,
if it was your first in 1,000 years…

09:47.378 --> 09:48.212
Yeah, what?

09:48.296 --> 09:50.590
Shouldn't you have gotten
a dental scaling first?

09:50.673 --> 09:51.507
Total jerk move.

09:54.844 --> 09:55.886
Dental scaling?

09:57.513 --> 09:58.598
What is that?

10:07.648 --> 10:09.525
Raise your hand if you feel discomfort…

10:10.026 --> 10:11.569
We haven't started yet.

10:12.069 --> 10:13.070
Say, "Ah."

10:15.865 --> 10:17.533
Bear with me for a moment.

10:27.793 --> 10:29.086
You don't have any money?

10:29.587 --> 10:30.588
And no ID?

10:31.339 --> 10:33.049
You treated him with no intake info?

10:33.132 --> 10:35.885
He said that he's a friend
of the auto shop owner, so…

10:35.968 --> 10:37.845
Ka-young? But I'm her only friend…

10:38.804 --> 10:40.306
Wait, are you the guy from the…

10:40.389 --> 10:42.600
-Middle East?
-Min-ji? I'm so happy to see you!

10:44.769 --> 10:48.397
I saw you eating gamja-tang together
at the gamja-tang place!

10:49.523 --> 10:53.653
Does seeing us eat gamja-tang together
excuse you from paying?

10:55.988 --> 10:56.822
A tab?

10:57.782 --> 10:59.075
Ridiculous, isn't it?

10:59.659 --> 11:01.077
It's outrageous, isn't it?

11:01.160 --> 11:03.204
Apparently, he doesn't have ID.

11:03.287 --> 11:04.914
And his name is none other than…

11:07.083 --> 11:08.334
Lee Beul-li.

11:08.417 --> 11:10.044
Lee Beul-li.

11:10.127 --> 11:13.714
That immediately killed my curiosity,
so I stopped asking questions.

11:13.798 --> 11:16.342
Do you even know anything
about this person?

11:17.510 --> 11:20.888
One thing I know for certain
is that he isn't human.

11:20.971 --> 11:23.391
No, of course he isn't.

11:23.474 --> 11:26.519
No decent human racks up a tab
with someone they just met.

11:27.353 --> 11:28.771
I'm feeling immense discomfort,

11:29.939 --> 11:31.065
so here are my hands.

11:31.148 --> 11:32.608
Seriously? I could just…

11:33.192 --> 11:36.028
Dr. Choi, we need to get
to the festival to volunteer.

11:36.112 --> 11:37.238
Okay. I'm coming.

11:38.572 --> 11:40.908
At this rate,
you'll wind up in big trouble.

11:41.742 --> 11:44.912
Snap out of it, Ms. Ki.

11:45.538 --> 11:49.083
Okay, so he has a decent face,
and he's pretty tall.

11:49.166 --> 11:51.043
And yeah, he has a velvety voice.

11:51.127 --> 11:53.462
Other than that,
what's he got going for him?

12:00.302 --> 12:02.513
It was essential given the rainy season.

12:03.889 --> 12:06.058
I'll pay you back
once I become a pro gamer…

12:06.892 --> 12:07.727
A pro gamer?

12:08.978 --> 12:11.397
You've lost every game
to the neighborhood kid.

12:11.897 --> 12:12.940
Pro gamer, you say?

12:14.567 --> 12:15.401
Come here.

12:23.200 --> 12:24.785
I dodged her pretty well today.

12:26.162 --> 12:27.788
I was only hit on one side.

12:46.474 --> 12:47.349
What the heck?

12:48.392 --> 12:49.393
Ms. Ki.

12:49.935 --> 12:52.062
Check the tire pressure for me, would you?

12:52.146 --> 12:53.022
Sure.

13:01.447 --> 13:02.406
You're drinking.

13:02.907 --> 13:04.325
Yes, that I am.

13:04.825 --> 13:07.620
And you're at the wheel
with the engine on.

13:07.703 --> 13:09.205
Yes, I'm at the wheel.

13:10.080 --> 13:10.915
Engine?

13:11.749 --> 13:12.583
What's that?

13:12.666 --> 13:13.793
All right, sir.

13:14.376 --> 13:15.503
Blow into this for us.

13:16.837 --> 13:18.380
And what's this? Is it a pipe?

13:18.464 --> 13:19.340
Go on.

13:21.634 --> 13:23.677
-Okay, more.
-More.

13:23.761 --> 13:28.057
-Harder.
-Harder!

13:29.767 --> 13:33.145
Hello, Homies!
It's Da-jin of Sky Farm Life.

13:33.646 --> 13:36.982
I'm coming to you today from
the Cheongpungho Cherry Blossom Festival.

13:37.483 --> 13:40.528
Let's start off by raiding
the For Daughter Strawberry stand.

13:41.111 --> 13:44.323
Guys, what do you call a strawberry
that was fired from its job?

13:44.406 --> 13:45.533
What?

13:45.616 --> 13:46.450
Berry upset!

13:49.912 --> 13:51.205
Right. "Berry upset!"

13:51.831 --> 13:53.582
You're hilarious!

13:54.291 --> 13:57.211
See that? Nothing flops for no reason.

13:57.294 --> 13:58.254
That was great.

13:58.337 --> 13:59.964
-Cherry blossoms!
-Indeed.

14:00.047 --> 14:01.799
Open wide. That's it.

14:02.800 --> 14:04.677
Can we try opening up a little wider?

14:04.760 --> 14:05.970
Even wider!

14:06.053 --> 14:08.097
Hello. We're from Cheongpungho Bank.

14:08.180 --> 14:10.558
We have a savings event,
so visit for a consultation.

14:12.268 --> 14:13.102
Hello.

14:17.648 --> 14:18.983
Where is the bathroom?

14:19.066 --> 14:20.860
Is the subway station close by?

14:20.943 --> 14:23.279
Without cilantro, please.

14:23.362 --> 14:24.572
What are you saying?

14:24.655 --> 14:25.865
Are you an Arab?

14:26.365 --> 14:28.534
You spoke Korean just fine earlier.

14:29.660 --> 14:31.245
He doesn't want any cilantro.

14:31.328 --> 14:32.204
What?

14:32.997 --> 14:36.125
Arabic was big back in school,
so I took it as my second language.

14:36.208 --> 14:37.710
I'll try speaking to him.

14:38.878 --> 14:40.754
My name is Oh Gyeong-yeol,

14:40.838 --> 14:42.798
a police officer
from the Republic of Korea.

14:42.882 --> 14:45.801
Sir, you have violated the traffic laws--

14:48.429 --> 14:49.263
Get over here.

14:49.346 --> 14:51.181
You said speaking Arabic would work.

14:51.265 --> 14:54.643
About that. It worked for me
toward the end of the Joseon dynasty…

14:55.603 --> 14:57.646
Just go. I'll handle things here.

14:58.147 --> 14:58.981
I could just…

15:04.904 --> 15:06.155
Oh Pan-geum!

15:06.822 --> 15:08.365
Buy that to eat. That one.

15:10.075 --> 15:12.411
Why are you walking around
eating raw tofu?

15:13.162 --> 15:14.955
I hear this is post-police food.

15:15.039 --> 15:17.875
Oh Pan-geum, you should drink
some black goat extract.

15:17.958 --> 15:19.084
To live a long life.

15:19.168 --> 15:22.630
I don't have that kind of money!
Why don't you buy me one, then?

15:23.839 --> 15:26.467
I can't buy things for you.
I only make recommendations.

15:26.550 --> 15:31.347
Honestly, I can't tell
if you're a bastard or just pitiful.

15:31.889 --> 15:32.723
Goodness me.

15:32.806 --> 15:34.600
-What?
-Hey, would you look at that?

15:35.309 --> 15:38.103
Goodness, that puppy
is bouncing around on its own.

15:38.187 --> 15:39.605
How incredible, no?

15:39.688 --> 15:42.191
-Wow. What is this?
-Come and have a look.

15:42.274 --> 15:43.692
-How adorable!
-It's walking!

15:43.776 --> 15:44.652
It's so cool.

15:46.320 --> 15:48.906
Hey, it's walking
but still stays in the same spot.

15:48.989 --> 15:49.949
How is that?

15:54.119 --> 15:56.080
At least her joints seem strong.

15:59.917 --> 16:00.751
My apologies.

16:04.004 --> 16:04.880
What is it?

16:07.841 --> 16:11.553
There's this thing called fireworks today.
Do you know when and where?

16:13.639 --> 16:17.184
The fireworks?
They'll be set off after the sun sets.

16:18.811 --> 16:20.688
You'd get the best view from there.

16:20.771 --> 16:21.605
Enjoy.

16:23.357 --> 16:25.025
The best view is that way?

16:36.870 --> 16:37.997
Ta-da.

16:40.457 --> 16:43.544
Damn, that fucker
looked like he was loaded.

16:44.044 --> 16:45.421
But he was broke, damn it.

16:45.504 --> 16:49.049
Well, well. Look at these motherfuckers
with no common decency.

16:49.133 --> 16:51.385
What do you think
you're doing on our turf?

16:51.468 --> 16:53.929
We thought we'd visit
the cherry blossom festival.

16:54.013 --> 16:55.472
The spring breeze is a-blowing.

16:55.556 --> 16:57.766
The cherry blossom festival is our turf.

16:57.850 --> 17:01.645
We didn't go against the current to invade
your cherry salmon festival, did we?

17:01.729 --> 17:03.814
You could always come to next year's.

17:03.897 --> 17:05.774
What, should we send you an invite?

17:05.858 --> 17:09.486
Great, you should all get prosthetics
while you're here.

17:09.570 --> 17:13.907
You know the health services
in Cheongpung are first-class.

17:16.660 --> 17:17.995
-What the…
-What the heck?

17:22.416 --> 17:25.461
What a relief! I almost got beat up
by the lump of clay again.

17:25.544 --> 17:27.337
And who's this prick?

17:27.421 --> 17:28.839
Hey, which gang are you from?

17:29.423 --> 17:31.550
-What?
-Why isn't he answering me?

17:31.633 --> 17:33.052
Just fucking wipe them all out!

17:37.973 --> 17:40.809
Darn it. I'm in the mood for flowers.

17:44.813 --> 17:47.316
-Damn you!
-Hey, you bastard!

18:06.043 --> 18:07.294
Wow.

18:07.377 --> 18:08.587
Goodness me.

18:08.670 --> 18:09.963
Oh boy.

18:11.423 --> 18:12.966
How stunning.

18:14.510 --> 18:17.554
AS SEXY
FUCK YOU

18:18.222 --> 18:19.056
What the…

18:21.350 --> 18:22.851
Goodness me, is that…

18:23.602 --> 18:25.521
Is that my Ka-young's name up there?

18:26.021 --> 18:29.108
"As, sexy, fuck, you"?

18:29.191 --> 18:31.068
Wait, what does that mean?

18:31.151 --> 18:33.028
So that prick does have money.

18:33.112 --> 18:35.030
KI KA-YOUNG
YOU'RE IN MY HEART

18:35.114 --> 18:37.407
So women really love those words?

18:37.491 --> 18:40.369
Yes, I told you.
Just trust me with these things.

18:40.953 --> 18:42.538
They go absolutely wild.

18:42.621 --> 18:44.498
She'll be corrupted in no time.

18:45.666 --> 18:46.708
Perfect.

18:56.844 --> 18:59.346
KI KA-YOUNG
FUCK YOU

19:00.764 --> 19:02.057
That son of a gun.

19:02.975 --> 19:05.394
That's what I always think
when I see Iblis too.

19:06.562 --> 19:08.313
I'm glad you relate, Ms. Ki Ka-young.

19:10.816 --> 19:14.069
What brings you here? You don't even
have a car since you can fly.

19:15.112 --> 19:17.656
Everyone in the village
is at the festival.

19:18.323 --> 19:19.700
I came as things are quiet.

19:20.367 --> 19:21.952
Do you have something to say to me?

19:22.494 --> 19:24.163
I won't return your feather.

19:25.789 --> 19:26.748
It's yours.

19:29.418 --> 19:31.211
What species are you, anyway?

19:31.712 --> 19:34.047
Just as there are Yorkshire terriers
and Chihuahuas,

19:34.131 --> 19:37.968
there are humans, angels, devils,
and genies. So which are you?

19:38.051 --> 19:41.180
I'm obviously his servant.
You saw my wings. I'm an angel.

19:41.972 --> 19:43.348
Right, an angel?

19:43.849 --> 19:47.060
I thought I'd double-check
since your wings were black.

19:48.270 --> 19:49.855
You do volunteer lunch runs, right?

19:50.898 --> 19:52.816
For a while, I've been thinking it's odd

19:52.900 --> 19:56.236
how every time you deliver lunch,
the elderly person

19:57.279 --> 19:58.322
ends up dead.

19:58.405 --> 20:02.743
I guess one could see it that way,
but try switching the order of events.

20:03.577 --> 20:07.039
I visit dying elders to bring them peace.

20:12.920 --> 20:13.795
I see.

20:15.214 --> 20:16.048
One more thing.

20:16.882 --> 20:21.136
Several of your buildings are within
a one-kilometer radius of my auto shop,

20:21.845 --> 20:24.223
and you never hid your identity from me.

20:25.349 --> 20:27.100
Are you spying on me?

20:27.851 --> 20:30.646
I am. To be more precise,
I'm working on his orders.

20:31.855 --> 20:33.523
What are they? His orders?

20:34.233 --> 20:38.278
"If there comes a moment that Iblis
bows his head before a human, you shall

20:39.112 --> 20:40.781
slit your brother's throat."

20:43.784 --> 20:44.868
Isn't that thrilling?

20:46.578 --> 20:50.415
That's why I'm going to do my best
to make sure Iblis doesn't win you over.

20:58.924 --> 20:59.925
It's too late.

21:01.718 --> 21:02.761
Pardon?

21:03.303 --> 21:05.013
Get lost so I can close shop.

21:06.181 --> 21:07.182
Right.

21:07.891 --> 21:08.976
Is that the time?

21:12.354 --> 21:14.064
But why are you being so rude?

21:14.147 --> 21:17.359
Who knows? Maybe because psychopaths
can't hide their displeasure?

21:17.442 --> 21:20.487
Or because you're trying to kill him
when I'm his master?

21:20.570 --> 21:21.405
Or maybe because

21:23.073 --> 21:24.574
he's already won me over.

21:26.243 --> 21:28.078
Which of these do you think it is?

21:35.669 --> 21:37.963
I knew I was right about her.

21:43.552 --> 21:45.012
A STUDY OF PSYCHOPATHS

21:45.095 --> 21:46.847
Did something happen?

21:47.472 --> 21:49.683
-I brought the books--
-Throw them out again.

21:50.183 --> 21:52.686
Psychopath? I'm absolutely certain!

21:54.271 --> 21:56.273
I should've known it was too lucky.

21:57.816 --> 22:00.694
At this rate, there's no telling
about her last two wishes.

22:01.695 --> 22:03.447
Should I have taken my scythe with me?

22:03.947 --> 22:06.491
She had the audacity
to tell me to "get lost."

22:06.575 --> 22:07.826
Like she was dismissing me!

22:07.909 --> 22:10.078
-To you, Master?
-Yes.

22:10.162 --> 22:12.331
You do look a little young for your age.

22:16.293 --> 22:18.795
Did you see the fireworks?
Weren't they cool?

22:18.879 --> 22:20.088
I did that, you know.

22:21.006 --> 22:22.299
Why did you choose that…

22:23.091 --> 22:24.926
Please, no!

22:25.427 --> 22:27.471
Hey, no using cheats like that!

22:27.554 --> 22:29.514
So you were behind the fireworks?

22:30.307 --> 22:31.141
Yes.

22:31.641 --> 22:34.186
I wondered
which crazy fool was behind them.

22:34.853 --> 22:35.687
Crazy what?

22:38.648 --> 22:41.401
Hey, where do you live?
Lead the way, punk.

22:41.485 --> 22:42.819
And where do you live?

22:43.904 --> 22:44.821
Lead the way.

22:47.574 --> 22:48.408
Pardon?

22:50.452 --> 22:52.120
The typical psychopath

22:53.330 --> 22:55.540
will harm others

22:56.375 --> 22:57.709
to get what they want.

22:58.210 --> 23:01.588
But my dear Ka-young
is a little different.

23:02.464 --> 23:05.926
Her grandma and the entire neighborhood
rallied to raise her with hope,

23:06.009 --> 23:08.178
so even though she may not feel guilt,

23:08.678 --> 23:11.473
she knows to stay
within her learned boundaries.

23:14.309 --> 23:15.727
All right. So what?

23:15.811 --> 23:18.480
So I'm saying I don't like you, you jerk.

23:19.481 --> 23:22.317
Ka-young will stay within those boundaries
no matter what,

23:23.235 --> 23:25.737
and I will protect Ka-young
as she does so.

23:26.655 --> 23:28.448
Whether it be psychologically…

23:32.494 --> 23:33.703
or physically.

23:35.872 --> 23:38.083
I'm her knight in shining armor, you see.

23:38.583 --> 23:39.793
You are, aren't you?

23:40.669 --> 23:44.005
All this time,
I thought you were a girl! Wow!

23:44.840 --> 23:46.091
This is on the house.

24:09.906 --> 24:11.158
Why are you laughing?

24:11.241 --> 24:13.201
Funniest thing I've heard in 983 years.

24:14.286 --> 24:15.704
Nine hundred and eighty…

24:16.496 --> 24:18.331
What the hell are you talking about?

24:19.875 --> 24:23.628
Now that we have a man in the mix,
you come to a seafood stew joint?

24:23.712 --> 24:25.088
I can't believe you.

24:25.172 --> 24:26.882
I didn't come. I just stopped by.

24:27.382 --> 24:29.801
I'll drop Min-ji off,
so I'll see you at home.

24:30.302 --> 24:31.428
Can't I take her home?

24:31.511 --> 24:33.889
We've actually bonded. Honestly. Master?

24:34.890 --> 24:36.391
Just call me "ma'am."

24:37.142 --> 24:38.685
Do you need anything else?

24:41.771 --> 24:42.689
Benevolence?

24:45.484 --> 24:47.986
Min-ji didn't pay before she left,
but I'm…

24:49.488 --> 24:50.739
I'm completely broke.

24:59.122 --> 25:01.249
I know about that. Allow me.

25:06.713 --> 25:07.839
I've reached 112, right?

25:08.798 --> 25:10.133
I'm turning myself in.

25:19.059 --> 25:20.685
Eating without paying? Seriously?

25:20.769 --> 25:24.689
This is unfair. I didn't even eat.
I just did the "not paying" part.

25:24.773 --> 25:25.732
Shut it.

25:26.233 --> 25:27.901
Why did you call me to bail you out?

25:27.984 --> 25:30.153
What about the one who's like you?
That angel!

25:32.280 --> 25:33.823
You're mistaken about that.

25:36.493 --> 25:39.746
Not only are Ejllael and I
different species, we're on bad terms.

25:39.829 --> 25:42.040
You and I are also on bad terms.

25:45.460 --> 25:46.920
What's with you lowering your voice?

25:47.003 --> 25:49.422
I may be Satan,
but this is no laughing matter.

25:51.383 --> 25:54.052
Ejllael and I fought a long battle.

25:55.679 --> 25:57.430
The war was devastating for me too.

25:58.390 --> 25:59.516
Why did you go to war?

26:07.857 --> 26:09.818
He created angels from light

26:10.986 --> 26:13.530
and genies from smokeless fire.

26:17.200 --> 26:20.579
The genies created from fire
grew increasingly arrogant,

26:21.413 --> 26:23.665
even aspiring to surpass Him.

26:26.585 --> 26:31.006
In his rage, he sent the angels
and ordered them to decimate us.

26:54.154 --> 26:57.532
The angels came down
and began slaughtering all the genies,

26:58.533 --> 27:01.786
and Ejllael led the charge.

27:07.042 --> 27:10.128
The war lasted 300 years,

27:10.712 --> 27:12.714
and I lost most of my brothers
as a result.

27:14.716 --> 27:18.053
So your quarrels turn into
full-blown wars of the gods?

27:18.553 --> 27:20.555
I've rarely seen my brothers since then.

27:22.307 --> 27:25.560
Partly because I defied his orders
and ended up in hell.

27:26.645 --> 27:30.523
And once released, I ended up trapped
for almost 1,000 years, so there's that.

27:33.360 --> 27:35.612
Where are your surviving brothers now?

27:38.073 --> 27:39.032
I'm not sure.

27:39.115 --> 27:42.160
They're probably inhabiting rings or lamps

27:43.161 --> 27:45.163
or living out their days in a pot.

27:47.082 --> 27:48.875
They may be controlling sleep…

27:56.424 --> 27:58.510
or tending to the flowers of souls.

28:07.185 --> 28:09.270
Or perhaps controlling the rain.

28:12.107 --> 28:13.274
One controls the rain?

28:17.195 --> 28:19.739
-What?
-Can't you find him? Find him and--

28:19.823 --> 28:21.408
Can't. No longer with us.

28:23.410 --> 28:25.120
I think Sade is looking for me.

28:29.708 --> 28:32.544
I'm pretty sure
Sade isn't looking for you.

29:03.283 --> 29:04.117
Wow.

29:15.920 --> 29:19.048
Miss, does the owner of this car
live in this neighborhood?

29:19.132 --> 29:19.966
Yes.

29:20.049 --> 29:21.593
Must be a crypto bro.

29:22.343 --> 29:23.678
I used to drive one of these.

29:24.345 --> 29:25.555
That's the 2024 model.

29:27.807 --> 29:28.975
Hey, come on!

29:29.058 --> 29:31.686
I said to patch the puncture,
not take the tire off!

29:32.604 --> 29:33.646
It needs to be changed.

29:34.230 --> 29:38.401
Did you even report all these?
Every one of these modifications?

29:38.485 --> 29:41.321
What are you, a civil servant?
Why would I report anything?

29:41.404 --> 29:42.614
Hey, put it back on.

29:46.117 --> 29:47.202
Where do you live?

29:48.536 --> 29:49.454
Why do you ask?

29:50.705 --> 29:51.748
Like what you see?

29:52.248 --> 29:54.542
Just concerned
you'll croak on your way home.

29:55.126 --> 29:56.628
Did you do these wheels yourself?

29:57.212 --> 29:59.339
You shoved them on
when they don't even fit.

29:59.422 --> 30:01.549
A simple patch-up wouldn't last an hour.

30:02.050 --> 30:05.136
I've explained everything,
so call a tow truck and take it away.

30:05.637 --> 30:06.638
I won't fix it.

30:07.722 --> 30:10.683
Is this how you treat your customers?
Hey, get over here.

30:21.069 --> 30:22.487
Is everything good?

30:23.279 --> 30:25.406
You drank that?

30:25.490 --> 30:27.826
There were so many bottles.
Weren't they for staff?

30:28.910 --> 30:30.745
No wonder they kept going missing.

30:31.871 --> 30:34.082
Wait, what were you saying?

30:35.375 --> 30:37.585
I was just asking
for the tow truck number.

30:38.545 --> 30:40.755
Zero, one, zero,

30:40.839 --> 30:43.258
six, three, four…

30:43.341 --> 30:44.968
-Wait, I didn't catch that.
-Two…

30:47.220 --> 30:48.638
Did you hit him?

30:53.393 --> 30:56.104
Six, three, four…

30:58.439 --> 31:01.109
What are you going to do
about this random, dreamy vibe?

31:02.193 --> 31:03.903
I'm sorry. I'll report everything.

31:03.987 --> 31:05.363
-I swear.
-Where are you going?

31:06.030 --> 31:07.824
-Damn it.
-Don't go.

31:07.907 --> 31:09.158
Hello, ma'am.

31:13.037 --> 31:15.373
-Hello.
-Thank you. Feel free to browse.

31:16.207 --> 31:17.834
Who's in charge of this display?

31:18.334 --> 31:20.003
Who's responsible for this station?

31:21.421 --> 31:22.297
Hey, you're back!

31:22.881 --> 31:24.424
I'm sorry, Im-seon.

31:24.507 --> 31:27.385
I had to step out for a moment.
My bowels were acting up again.

31:28.553 --> 31:31.848
Don't you think it's wrong
to call your branch manager by name?

31:33.182 --> 31:35.310
At our age, we're all a little unwell.

31:35.393 --> 31:37.520
Is it too much to ask you to do your job?

31:40.899 --> 31:42.901
I can't take any more of this crap.

31:43.443 --> 31:45.570
Ms. Jung Yeong-sun. What did you just say?

31:46.779 --> 31:50.533
I said I can't stand it anymore.
This is so ridiculous that I quit.

31:50.617 --> 31:52.201
Im-seon, this is just wrong.

31:52.285 --> 31:54.370
Has the late promotion gone to your head?

31:54.454 --> 31:55.622
Ms. Jung Yeong-sun!

31:55.705 --> 31:57.707
I don't know how you were even promoted,

31:57.790 --> 32:00.001
but is this how you treat your coworkers?

32:00.084 --> 32:02.962
We've all heard the rumors
about you taking bribes from vendors.

32:03.046 --> 32:04.589
Do we look like fools?

32:04.672 --> 32:06.215
Yeong-sun, please!

32:08.092 --> 32:09.594
How could I be so stupid?

32:10.178 --> 32:13.056
I shouldn't have asked to be
a branch manager at this age.

32:13.139 --> 32:15.767
People look down on me,
and I keep making mistakes.

32:20.772 --> 32:22.774
I guess I could get to it a bit quicker.

32:24.484 --> 32:25.485
Excuse me?

32:26.527 --> 32:27.904
Here's my second wish.

32:28.571 --> 32:30.239
Take me back 20 years

32:30.823 --> 32:32.450
and make me branch manager then.

32:34.369 --> 32:37.956
If I'd made branch manager back then,
just imagine all the money.

32:46.297 --> 32:49.217
Shall we go, then?
Twenty years into the past?

33:09.028 --> 33:11.489
BRANCH MANAGER
KANG IM-SEON

33:14.409 --> 33:17.161
Go through that door,
and it will be 20 years in the past,

33:17.870 --> 33:20.123
and you will still be the branch manager.

33:29.590 --> 33:30.425
Talk to me.

33:56.909 --> 34:00.204
Why are you alone?
Where's Dad? He said he'd pick you up.

34:00.997 --> 34:02.498
Dad has work to do.

34:06.377 --> 34:07.462
Long time no see.

34:08.046 --> 34:10.256
Do you still like hot chamomile tea?

34:10.339 --> 34:13.509
Yes. I'm still a psychopath,
so caffeine isn't good for me.

34:17.555 --> 34:18.931
You haven't changed a bit.

34:19.015 --> 34:21.601
I thought you'd at least ask,
"What brings you here?"

34:22.185 --> 34:24.145
I moved here with my wife and son.

34:24.228 --> 34:27.523
Take good care of us. I found out
about this place thanks to you.

34:29.275 --> 34:33.196
I don't recall ever telling you
exactly where I live.

34:33.279 --> 34:36.657
Not many University of Science grads
run auto shops.

34:37.366 --> 34:38.701
I guess.

34:38.785 --> 34:42.038
Either way, it's good to see you again.
You look great.

34:42.663 --> 34:43.831
How's business?

34:47.752 --> 34:49.462
True joy.

35:05.144 --> 35:07.897
I guess the house looked
pretty much the same 20 years ago.

35:11.109 --> 35:12.318
Except for you.

35:36.384 --> 35:40.054
You grow up to be super pretty
20 years from now.

35:40.638 --> 35:42.890
So careful with this.
You wouldn't want to hurt…

35:47.728 --> 35:48.771
What is it?

35:49.480 --> 35:51.315
Someone just entered my memory.

35:56.154 --> 35:59.073
Grandma told me not to speak to strangers.

36:00.950 --> 36:02.118
Leave!

36:02.201 --> 36:03.661
Wait, no!

36:03.744 --> 36:04.954
Hey, you startled me.

36:06.247 --> 36:08.457
So you're clearly as odd as ever.

36:11.919 --> 36:14.172
"So you're clearly as odd as ever."

36:16.299 --> 36:18.217
He was sleazy as hell.

36:18.718 --> 36:20.845
So how did you hurt your head again?

36:23.097 --> 36:24.223
Who else would it be?

36:25.433 --> 36:27.310
She was even worse 20 years ago.

36:27.393 --> 36:29.437
Did you visit the past for a wish?

36:30.104 --> 36:31.189
Yeah.

36:49.874 --> 36:52.168
That'll be 18,000 won.

36:55.630 --> 36:58.216
I need to see your ID for the alcohol…

37:17.693 --> 37:18.611
Ms. Ki!

37:18.694 --> 37:20.780
What's wrong? Is something up?

37:21.614 --> 37:23.366
Just that it's raining.

37:25.076 --> 37:26.244
Keep up the good work.

37:34.835 --> 37:36.671
Where the hell is he?

37:42.301 --> 37:43.386
Wait, what?

37:43.469 --> 37:44.595
Why is it stopping?

37:46.180 --> 37:47.723
But it's the rainy season!

38:00.486 --> 38:02.446
Where the hell were you? It rained!

38:02.947 --> 38:05.449
Do you know how long
I looked everywhere for you?

38:05.950 --> 38:06.784
Seriously?

38:06.867 --> 38:08.244
Hey, you're the one

38:09.120 --> 38:10.997
who took a rock this big, you know.

38:11.080 --> 38:14.000
You do all that,
then I hear about you acting all "odd."

38:14.083 --> 38:16.210
You're deflecting because you're cornered.

38:16.294 --> 38:19.005
I'm in a corner? Who was the jerk
who came by the auto shop?

38:19.588 --> 38:21.549
I heard you were giggling with each other.

38:21.632 --> 38:24.302
Kiss me or crack my skull,
but just do one.

38:24.385 --> 38:26.595
You can't do both, you serial kisser!

38:26.679 --> 38:27.513
I can't?

38:28.597 --> 38:31.058
Then I choose to crack your skull.
Come here.

38:31.142 --> 38:33.394
Hey, come on. You're my master.

38:35.855 --> 38:37.481
Shush. We're talking right now.

38:38.149 --> 38:39.900
Come on. Treat me with care.

38:39.984 --> 38:41.277
Take care of me.

38:41.944 --> 38:42.903
I said shush!

38:42.987 --> 38:46.574
Why does every damn dog around here
bark like mad whenever they see you?

38:46.657 --> 38:48.826
They're just scared I'll take them in.

38:49.535 --> 38:52.580
They need to read human expressions,
but I don't have any.

38:53.080 --> 38:55.583
Hey, I don't plan on taking you in either!

39:08.929 --> 39:09.972
Sade!

39:17.355 --> 39:20.733
I am Genie, the lamp spirit.
…shall grant you three wishes…

39:20.816 --> 39:22.234
…no traveling to the future.

39:22.318 --> 39:23.486
Anything besides that,

39:23.569 --> 39:25.196
your wish… is my command.

39:27.031 --> 39:28.407
But before that,

39:28.908 --> 39:32.078
tell all the dogs in the area
to stop barking at Ki Ka-young.

39:32.703 --> 39:34.538
If they bark one more time,

39:34.622 --> 39:37.166
I'll change every last one of you
into cats.

39:38.167 --> 39:39.085
Tell him.

39:43.172 --> 39:44.048
Ki Ka-young.

39:48.636 --> 39:52.264
MUTT, AGE 7
MADE FIRST WISH ON MAY 16, 2024

39:52.348 --> 39:54.433
TO BECOME A PERSON, WITH SPECIFICS

39:54.517 --> 39:57.395
CHARMING MIDDLE-AGED MAN IN HIS 40S
WHO RESEMBLES DANIEL HENNEY

39:57.978 --> 40:00.022
Now that's not a face
you see in these parts.

40:01.190 --> 40:02.191
Is there a film shoot?

40:02.274 --> 40:04.527
Remember I was depressed
about losing my eyesight with age?

40:04.610 --> 40:07.363
-Yeah?
-I think I just fully recovered.

40:07.446 --> 40:09.448
-Let's go, Yeong-sun.
-Sure.

40:10.032 --> 40:10.866
Wow.

40:30.761 --> 40:31.637
I'm hungry.

40:32.138 --> 40:33.013
Chicken and beer?

40:33.097 --> 40:35.141
Sounds good. Let's do it.

40:38.310 --> 40:41.063
Suit and slicked back hair.
Wow, he's doggone handsome.

40:41.147 --> 40:42.523
He's coming this way.

40:42.606 --> 40:44.525
Hand me some blotting paper and lip tint.

41:01.876 --> 41:04.086
-What's he doing?
-He must be crazy!

41:04.712 --> 41:05.838
My gosh!

41:05.921 --> 41:08.674
They say handsome men
are either gay or dogs.

41:09.800 --> 41:11.218
His actions clearly show

41:12.344 --> 41:13.345
he's a total mutt.

41:24.523 --> 41:25.941
You've run out of water.

41:33.157 --> 41:34.700
Don't skip breakfast tomorrow.

41:40.331 --> 41:41.165
Pardon?

41:44.376 --> 41:46.504
The food doesn't taste good.

41:47.004 --> 41:48.255
It's too bland.

41:50.299 --> 41:51.884
It's too bland for you?

41:52.885 --> 41:55.221
I should have been
more generous with the salt.

41:57.932 --> 41:59.016
I was only joking.

42:01.310 --> 42:05.105
What will happen to me now?

42:06.690 --> 42:08.192
A question I'm tired of getting.

42:11.278 --> 42:12.905
One thing's for certain.

42:13.614 --> 42:15.699
I'll be saving on the cost of salt.

42:42.268 --> 42:43.352
Yes, Grandma?

42:43.435 --> 42:45.980
Ka-young, you're not seeing
things again, are you?

42:46.063 --> 42:49.108
You're taking your meds, right?
Every dose without missing any?

42:49.191 --> 42:51.735
Yes, you see me take them every day. Why?

42:52.236 --> 42:55.906
If you have any wishes, just tell me.
I'll make them all come true.

42:56.407 --> 42:57.825
Wishes?

42:57.908 --> 42:59.827
What is this in the notebook in your room?

42:59.910 --> 43:02.788
Did you like Daniel Henney?

43:04.456 --> 43:06.542
You can see that?

43:08.294 --> 43:09.295
She can see that?

43:10.254 --> 43:14.049
Wait, was it always visible
to everyone else's eyes?

43:14.133 --> 43:15.676
You're seriously asking me that?

43:15.759 --> 43:18.596
This damn magic has way too many holes.

43:20.180 --> 43:21.140
This won't do.

43:21.223 --> 43:24.018
We need a safe space
to hide the notebook and pen.

43:24.101 --> 43:24.935
Your lamp.

43:25.686 --> 43:28.105
Are you sure
only you and Sade can get in?

43:29.315 --> 43:32.151
If they really wanted to,
Ejllael or Irem probably could.

43:32.234 --> 43:33.485
But even you couldn't.

43:33.569 --> 43:34.987
So it must be safe.

43:36.447 --> 43:39.408
What does it look like inside the lamp?
Is it cozy?

43:41.994 --> 43:42.995
It's dismal.

44:04.433 --> 44:05.559
Do you see this?

44:05.643 --> 44:09.772
Do you get a sense of how lonely
I must have been for 983 years?

44:09.855 --> 44:11.815
Sorry, but I don't know
what loneliness is.

44:13.359 --> 44:14.652
But you do know to be sorry?

44:15.694 --> 44:16.779
Of course I don't.

44:17.363 --> 44:20.407
But Min-ji told me that leading with that
makes me seem considerate.

44:22.743 --> 44:24.328
And you know what considerate is?

44:24.411 --> 44:25.788
Yes. That one's quite easy.

44:26.288 --> 44:29.667
I just need to be honest.
For instance, it's something like this.

44:30.250 --> 44:32.169
I heard it all from that brother of yours.

44:32.252 --> 44:35.756
That you'll get your throat slit
if you bow your head to a righteous human.

44:36.256 --> 44:37.633
Ejllael, that prick!

44:38.967 --> 44:40.636
That was considerate? Not a threat?

44:41.261 --> 44:42.513
Are you seriously not

44:43.806 --> 44:44.682
scared of me?

44:44.765 --> 44:46.767
To be honest, I don't know what fear is.

44:47.309 --> 44:49.436
But Grandma did say
that apathy is the scariest.

44:50.688 --> 44:53.899
My grandma is an incredibly fragile
safety feature to my apathy.

44:54.400 --> 44:55.776
If that safety feature…

44:57.695 --> 44:58.779
were to disappear,

44:59.279 --> 45:01.573
there's a chance
my violence would take over,

45:01.657 --> 45:03.075
so I'm making preparations.

45:03.158 --> 45:04.910
But you'd know all that from spying on me.

45:06.120 --> 45:08.080
"As natural a death as possible."

45:08.914 --> 45:10.165
I do know, yes.

45:10.249 --> 45:14.420
Like deep-sea equipment failure
or a fall on a remote trail.

45:16.213 --> 45:19.800
But why do all that when you don't have
emotions or any affection for humans?

45:19.883 --> 45:22.886
I am a stone in a shoe
to the people of the world.

45:23.971 --> 45:25.723
I make people uncomfortable.

45:25.806 --> 45:28.100
So I'm removing that stone for them.

45:29.685 --> 45:30.728
For my grandma.

45:32.980 --> 45:36.650
So if you're going to kill me, hurry.
And don't go getting your throat slit.

45:41.739 --> 45:43.073
Ejllael?

45:43.866 --> 45:46.744
The more I see that angel,
the less I like him.

45:47.369 --> 45:50.956
-Whatever you do, don't lose to him.
-Wait, you're actually taking my side?

45:51.749 --> 45:54.710
-Shouldn't I?
-You shouldn't. If you do, then…

45:55.377 --> 45:56.211
You know?

45:56.712 --> 45:57.588
I'm going to wring

45:59.089 --> 46:00.340
your neck.

46:00.883 --> 46:02.468
That would make things strange.

46:02.551 --> 46:04.011
We're already strange.

46:04.720 --> 46:07.014
You and I are both antisocial,

46:07.514 --> 46:10.058
so why am I under scrutiny
while you're admired?

46:13.687 --> 46:16.940
What exactly was his purpose
in making you and me meet?

46:20.110 --> 46:21.153
That's it.

46:24.156 --> 46:26.533
I should have been pondering that.

46:27.284 --> 46:28.368
Not totally clueless.

46:31.663 --> 46:33.040
Okay, we need furniture.

46:33.874 --> 46:36.960
Bring over the table and chairs
I made in the workshop.

46:48.430 --> 46:50.766
No matter which way I look at it,

46:50.849 --> 46:52.726
I don't think you made these.

46:53.310 --> 46:55.771
They seem to be made
by a giant corporation.

46:55.854 --> 46:59.399
Don't talk back!
You now have two pieces of furniture.

47:01.735 --> 47:04.071
It'd be nice to have another rug,
wouldn't it?

47:18.168 --> 47:19.711
This way. Here.

47:24.508 --> 47:26.009
Starting the cleaning cycle.

47:32.558 --> 47:33.642
Why the hell is this…

47:33.725 --> 47:37.604
Is this used to fix things
or to destroy them?

47:38.355 --> 47:39.731
That all depends on you.

47:42.150 --> 47:43.527
Hey!

47:45.487 --> 47:48.782
Go that way, and you won't come back.
It'd take over 1,000 years.

47:49.283 --> 47:50.242
That thing.

47:56.999 --> 47:58.542
It's coming together.

47:59.167 --> 48:00.794
Now I feel somewhat reassured.

48:04.214 --> 48:06.049
About Ms. Im-seon.

48:07.426 --> 48:10.554
She could have done whatever she wanted
beyond the supermarket,

48:11.179 --> 48:13.974
so I wonder why
she didn't just leave the supermarket.

48:14.600 --> 48:16.059
That's how humans are.

48:16.935 --> 48:20.188
They dream of being king
but fear leaving their domain.

48:20.689 --> 48:24.568
They've seen how kings rule by force,
and so they wish for the same.

48:25.527 --> 48:27.654
That's the cowardly nature of humans

48:28.405 --> 48:30.324
and the reason why I hate them.

48:40.000 --> 48:43.503
He may not be clueless,
but he's also not big on enlightenment.

48:45.088 --> 48:46.381
Humans hate you too.

48:47.841 --> 48:49.676
So that's another use for that.

48:51.303 --> 48:55.474
If I killed you on behalf of all humans,
would I go to heaven?

48:56.558 --> 48:58.185
You think it would end at that?

48:58.977 --> 49:00.729
He'd give you heaven if you asked.

49:01.313 --> 49:02.689
Come here. Get over here.

49:03.273 --> 49:06.735
Come here.

49:08.862 --> 49:09.780
Get over here.

49:11.156 --> 49:12.616
-I said come.
-I don't want to.

49:12.699 --> 49:14.159
I LAUGH IN MY DREAMS, JOYFULLY

49:14.242 --> 49:16.662
-Let's keep it humane and…
-But you're not human.

49:18.372 --> 49:20.707
Where is that mumbling coming from?

49:23.502 --> 49:27.339
I can hear sound coming from this.
Is it a radio?

49:29.091 --> 49:30.175
Pan-geum!

49:30.676 --> 49:32.469
Pan-geum, are you home?

49:32.552 --> 49:33.887
Yes, I'm here!

49:35.430 --> 49:38.100
Goodness, you came all this way
in the pouring rain?

49:46.191 --> 49:47.192
I think she said…

49:49.277 --> 49:50.654
it's raining.

49:53.240 --> 49:55.867
It seems that way, doesn't it?

49:56.868 --> 49:58.328
Do you have any alcohol here?

50:01.289 --> 50:02.124
Should I buy some?

50:04.710 --> 50:06.545
Wouldn't it be faster…

50:08.547 --> 50:09.381
to go together?

50:12.092 --> 50:14.011
Don't forget we need money to buy alcohol.

50:14.094 --> 50:16.430
-This is all I need.
-You'll use that as collateral?

50:18.515 --> 50:22.185
-My goodness. What shall we do?
-Grandma?

50:22.269 --> 50:24.563
Grandma, why are you crying?

50:24.646 --> 50:26.023
-Good heavens.
-What is it?

50:27.024 --> 50:28.150
Why is she crying?

50:28.233 --> 50:31.403
We just heard
that the craftsman, Mr. Kim, died.

50:31.486 --> 50:34.573
You know, the man
who taught you how to carve wood.

50:35.449 --> 50:37.325
Then why is my grandma crying?

50:37.409 --> 50:39.786
She's crying because she's sad.

50:39.870 --> 50:41.830
She's sad that her friend died.

50:41.913 --> 50:43.665
This is exactly why, you know.

50:43.749 --> 50:45.542
Why people call you a psycho.

50:45.625 --> 50:46.460
Heung-rye!

50:46.543 --> 50:47.377
What?

50:48.086 --> 50:51.256
Goodness me!

50:51.339 --> 50:57.262
Death makes life seem so futile.

50:57.763 --> 51:02.642
It brings me to tears.

51:18.825 --> 51:20.994
My goodness.

51:21.078 --> 51:23.705
It's so tragic. I can't bear it.

51:23.789 --> 51:27.000
How can you
cast the world aside like this?

51:28.710 --> 51:32.172
Even so, they say he passed peacefully
as if drifting off to sleep.

51:32.255 --> 51:33.965
Consider that a good death.

51:34.049 --> 51:36.301
There's no such thing as a good death.

51:37.803 --> 51:41.640
I guess you kids would have no idea,
with your entire lives ahead of you.

51:43.975 --> 51:46.311
I'm not afraid of dying,

51:46.812 --> 51:50.690
but if I think of my darling Ka-young…

51:53.527 --> 51:56.446
What if my heart suddenly stops

51:57.322 --> 51:59.574
or I have a stroke and collapse?

52:00.075 --> 52:03.578
What if I get cancer and diabetes
and end up with dementia too?

52:03.662 --> 52:08.458
Good heavens,
how would she ever take care of me?

52:09.126 --> 52:11.419
Why would you think such silly thoughts?

52:12.379 --> 52:16.466
At that moment, I realized that Grandma
must have read the same articles as me.

52:17.050 --> 52:19.177
"An aging society is coming fast."

52:19.261 --> 52:21.471
"Prepare yourself
for age-related illness."

52:22.097 --> 52:23.807
"Medical Tomorrow."

52:24.766 --> 52:26.518
I was going to die if Grandma died,

52:26.601 --> 52:27.936
but Grandma actually wants

52:28.603 --> 52:30.564
to live a long and healthy life.

52:31.690 --> 52:33.233
So your point is?

52:36.069 --> 52:37.571
I'll make my second wish.

52:41.575 --> 52:44.244
Make my grandma young.

52:44.744 --> 52:45.871
The same age as me.

52:47.998 --> 52:50.667
This is my second wish.

56:22.045 --> 56:27.050
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
